  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-1].$ It is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-1)$ and also left continuous at $x=-1.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $[-2,0]$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $[-1,\\infty ).$ Although the function is continuous on $(-1,\\infty ),$ it is not right-continuous at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
